.TH ESL-SIMILAR 1 "March 2026" "ecoSignalLab 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
esl-similar \- find most similar files in a corpus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esl similar
.I query.wav
.I corpus_dir
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare one query file to a folder of candidates and rank by distance.
Supports feature, single-metric, and multi-metric similarity modes.
.SH MODES
.TP
\fB\-\-mode auto|feature|metric|metrics\fR
Select comparison mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-metric\fR \fIID\fR
Metric ID for single-metric mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fILIST\fR
Metric list for multi-metric mode.
.SH DISTANCE FUNCTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-distance cosine\fR
Cosine distance.
.TP
\fB\-\-distance euclidean\fR
Euclidean distance.
.TP
\fB\-\-distance manhattan\fR
Manhattan distance.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-top-k\fR \fIN\fR
Number of results.
.TP
\fB\-\-feature-set\fR \fIauto|core|librosa|all\fR
Feature backend in feature mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fIPATH\fR
Output JSON ranking.
.TP
\fB\-\-csv\fR \fIPATH\fR
Output CSV ranking.
.SH EXAMPLE
.B esl similar query.wav corpus_dir --mode auto --distance cosine --top-k 10 --json out/similarity.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esl (1)
